# ArticleCompanyCTA

## Purpose
A centered call to action with a subtle background, heading, description, prominent link, and optional note. Use it for newsletter signups, demo requests, or contact links. Limit it to one per article.

## HTML Inputs
Static HTML needs no imports or runtime props. Edit the text, attributes, and classes directly in the `.html` file.

| Input | Type | Required | Default | HTML mapping |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `title` | `string` | Yes | — | Heading text in `<h2>` |
| `body` | `string` | Yes | — | Description in `<p class="cta__body">` |
| `buttonText` | `string` | Yes | — | Visible link label |
| `buttonHref` | `string` | Yes | — | Destination in the link’s `href` |
| `note` | `string` | No | — | Text in `<p class="cta__note">` below the link; omit the element if unused |
| `id` | `string` | No | — | Unique section `id` for fragment links |
| `className` | `string` | No | — | Extra classes appended to the section’s `class` |
| `buttonVariant` | `primary` or `secondary` | No | `primary` | Use `cta__link` for primary; add `cta__link--secondary` for secondary |

## Semantic Hints
`cta`, `company-cta`, `promo`, `action-block`, `conversion`, `call-to-action`, `promotion`, `signup`

## Structure and Styling
Use a `<section>` with a centered, width-constrained wrapper containing a heading, description, styled anchor, and optional note. Match the site’s existing CTA or card background, border, radius, shadow, and padding rather than using a generic gray panel. Use a bold heading, readable line spacing, muted supporting text, and a prominent brand-colored link.

## Accessibility
Reference the heading’s unique `id` with `aria-labelledby`. Keep the CTA an anchor because it navigates. Use a descriptive link label, sufficient contrast for all text, and a visible keyboard focus indicator.

## Complete Example — `article.html`

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Newsletter CTA</title>
  <style>
    .cta {
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid #bfd9e8;
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: #eef8ff;
      color: #132b3e;
      text-align: center;
      font: 1rem/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif;
    }
    .cta__content { max-width: 38rem; margin-inline: auto; }
    .cta h2 { margin: 0; line-height: 1.2; }
    .cta__body, .cta__note { color: #425668; }
    .cta__link {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: .75rem 1.25rem;
      border: 2px solid #075980;
      border-radius: .5rem;
      background: #075980;
      color: #fff;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .cta__link--secondary { background: transparent; color: #075980; }
    .cta__link:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #132b3e; outline-offset: 4px; }
    .cta__note { margin: .75rem 0 0; font-size: .875rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <section class="cta" id="newsletter-cta" aria-labelledby="newsletter-heading">
    <div class="cta__content">
      <h2 id="newsletter-heading">Stay Updated on AI Trends</h2>
      <p class="cta__body">Get weekly AI insights and best practices in your inbox.</p>
      <a class="cta__link" href="/newsletter">Subscribe to Newsletter</a>
      <p class="cta__note">No spam. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</body>
</html>
```

