# ArticleTocPlaceholder

## Purpose
An empty HTML `<div>` that marks where an article’s table of contents (TOC) should appear. A plain JavaScript article enhancer finds the slot by its `data-article-toc-placeholder` attribute and inserts the TOC using DOM APIs. No framework or imports are required.

## Props (HTML configuration)
**Required props:** None. Always include `data-article-toc-placeholder` on the slot so the enhancer can find it.

| Optional prop | Type | Default | Static HTML equivalent |
|---|---|---|---|
| `className` | `string` | — | Add CSS classes with the `class` attribute. |
| `noMargin` | `boolean` | `false` | Add the `toc-no-margin` class to remove default margins. |

## Semantic Hints
`toc-placeholder`, `sidebar-toc`, `toc-wrapper`, `toc-slot`, `toc-container`

## Behavior and Accessibility
1. Start with an empty slot marked `hidden`.
2. If the article has enough headings for a TOC, insert a `<nav aria-label="Table of contents">` with links to their IDs, then remove `hidden`. The `<nav>` provides the navigation landmark without an explicit `role`.
3. If no TOC is generated, leave the slot empty and hidden so it takes up no space and creates no landmark.

## Placement and Styling
Place the slot near the top of a long article: inline before the first section (especially on mobile), in a sticky desktop sidebar, or in a fixed panel with a toggle button. Keep its width aligned with the article or sidebar column. When populated, use a rounded border and subtle background that match the article styling.

## Complete Example (`article.html`)

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Planning a Garden</title>
  <style>
    article { max-width: 65ch; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
    [data-article-toc-placeholder] {
      margin-block: 1rem;
      padding: 1rem;
      border: 1px solid #d5dad6;
      border-radius: .5rem;
      background: #f5f7f5;
    }
    .toc-no-margin[data-article-toc-placeholder] { margin: 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <article>
      <h1>Planning a Garden</h1>
      <div data-article-toc-placeholder class="toc-no-margin" hidden></div>
      <section>
        <h2 id="site">Choose a site</h2>
        <p>Look for a spot with enough sunlight.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 id="soil">Prepare the soil</h2>
        <p>Loosen compacted soil before planting.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <script>
    for (const slot of document.querySelectorAll('[data-article-toc-placeholder]')) {
      const headings = slot.closest('article')?.querySelectorAll('h2[id]');
      if (!headings || headings.length < 2) continue;

      const nav = document.createElement('nav');
      nav.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Table of contents');
      const list = document.createElement('ul');

      for (const heading of headings) {
        const item = document.createElement('li');
        const link = document.createElement('a');
        link.href = '#' + encodeURIComponent(heading.id);
        link.textContent = heading.textContent;
        item.append(link);
        list.append(item);
      }

      nav.append(list);
      slot.append(nav);
      slot.hidden = false;
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

